{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/254337-the-lost-and-the-dreaming","id":254337,"title":"The Lost and the Dreaming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-11T10:49:33-07:00","id":254337,"title":"The Lost and the Dreaming","content":"With Changeling: the Dreaming 20th Anniversary more or less confirmed, might we be seeing a Changeling Translation Guide sometime in the future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T11:08:12-07:00","id":254426,"title":"","content":"To be honest, unless you plan on making Lost and Dreamers antagonists of each other (Charlatans and Dauntain), I have no idea how you would even begin to pull that off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T12:16:29-07:00","id":287904,"title":"","content":"They are such different games I don't think you can do such a thing. What I would love to see is a guide to using the nwod mechanics for the dreaming setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T12:37:41-07:00","id":287915,"title":"","content":"Eh, you could use it to import mechanics you like one to the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T12:52:02-07:00","id":287941,"title":"","content":"I'm sort of fond of Dauntain, so I found this (unfinished) homebrew amusing.<br /> <b>Court of Iron</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>The mind is a machine. Or the product of a machine, the brain. You know this to be true. What you and I experienced was nothing more nor less than a protracted malfunction. There is a process to fix things. It may seem... fanciful, at first, but I assure you, it's temporary. Soon, we can put all fantasy behind us. Which will you trust: The false ephemera of dreams, or cold, solid Iron?</i><br /> </span></span></span><ul><li>Emotion - Closure</li> <li>Associations - Banality, order, stability, reality, guns, metal, gray, community, swords, technology, humanity, normalcy, mundanity, solidarity, denial.</li> <li>Contracts of Crystalization - Forcing a fixed form on ideas, concepts, and eventually reality. Shutting down Hedge gates.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T19:33:26-07:00","id":288163,"title":"","content":"Actually, thinking on it, I would love to see DREAMING V LOST WHOEVER WINS WE LOSE. It'd be a unique way to do a translation guide and would probably wind up working out for a lot of people just because of the sheer divisiveness between the two lines.<br /> <br /> Or you could try to do like a crossover of themes or something, I guess. Like a Dreaming game with more of a Lost-style focus on the fact that you're probably insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T20:23:22-07:00","id":288192,"title":"","content":"You know, I've seen this pop up a lot, but I've never seen what people would use in one or the other game.<br /> <br /> So, brass tacks time: what would you use from <i>Dreaming</i> in <i>Lost</i> and visa versa?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-20-2014, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T00:40:28-07:00","id":288412,"title":"","content":"I'd like to use the BYO Faerie from Lost a lot: pick a Seeming, Pick a Kith (or two) pick a Court, and you sort of mix and match bonuses and faerie powers without going full powers list. You can organize what you get extra dice or 9- agains to to make, to some degree, a Faerie like you like without just consulting a long list of powers...Seemings and Kiths have stereotypes, and Changelings of the same Kith or whatever may associate it. Dreaming you get a set of powers (usually cool, at least if you are Kithian, Thallain or Adhene) but no mixing or matching unless you go for a Noble House, which is unusually outside Sidhe or Mer.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, some Kith powers I really like don't have anything similar in Lost. One of my players still is upset she can't make a &quot;proper&quot; Goblin like the Thallain, and some of the Adhene powers appeal to me that were never translated also. So some of that could be welcome.<br /> <br /> It's not something I, personally, would run, but a shard combining them where Kithain are, essentially, Gentry reincarnated so much they have been humanized trying to save links to Arcadia with Lost being essentially just the same would be...interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T07:41:33-07:00","id":288528,"title":"","content":"As lovely a dream as <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b> is, my experience has always been that Chimerical Reality makes it a monstrous nightmare to try to play. The only thing I might 'port over in either direction would be to drop the separated Chimerical Reality from Mundane Reality of Dreaming and make it the Mask from Lost. Those dragons are really there, not just on some pseudo-imaginary plane. The Dreaming can be like the Umbra/Shadow for the werewolves - a place of power and a place that's almost as much &quot;home&quot; as the real world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T09:55:34-07:00","id":288642,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I run into similar issues, except I actually <i>like</i> chimerical reality despite the troubles it presents in running the game.<br /> <br /> The Changeling games might be the only ones I wouldn't mix or cross from Old to New. Which is weird because of them are my favorites in each respectively.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, so there is a minor temptation to port the old system over into the new one, but my theory is that unless you can get something out of throwing the two types of protagonists together or mixing them, the point's a little moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-21-2014, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T10:00:46-07:00","id":288651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/254337-the-lost-and-the-dreaming?p=288642#post288642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I run into similar issues, except I actually <i>like</i> chimerical reality despite the troubles it presents in running the game.<br /> <br /> The Changeling games might be the only ones I wouldn't mix or cross from Old to New. Which is weird because of them are my favorites in each respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked it, too. Not only is it a fascinating concept and very high brow to place in an RPG, but a brilliant meta-commentary on the nature of role-playing in general.<br /> <br /> <b>BUT, IT'S A BITCH TO RUN!</b><br /> <br /> It's a hell of a book keeping job to know when it's Mundane, Chimerical or Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T12:10:50-07:00","id":288737,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dreaming's major issue was that it could not decide what was it's main theme ultimately. Its premise was <span style=\"color:#252525\">executed poorly as the writers were sort of all over the place as to what they actually wanted the game to be about. Is it a hopeful game of restoring beauty and glamour to the world? Is it a grimdark game of coping living in a world where you see and feel the magic slowly dying? Damn if I know.<br /> <br /> Basically, C20 should get more consistent direction and any port should be based on C20 material since I don't think pre-20 is consistent enough for porting wholesale.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-26-2014, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T13:07:11-07:00","id":288817,"title":"","content":"We have a player who loves Lost and hated Dreaming because of the question of if the Changeling form was real or not. I always thought it was odd he hated one and liked the other so much. I do prefer how Lost handles the double reality.<br /> <br /> I ran two good long term (measured in years) games of Dreaming, but sadly the Adhene did not show up in books till the very end of the second, so I never got to use them in a successful game. I ran three different Dreaming games after, but they all had major problems. I think one ran close to a year, but it was so fraught with issues I can't call it successful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:07:27-07:00","id":288988,"title":"","content":"I think a CtL setting with our world, arcadia,the hedge .. but, the Hedge is the dreaming and Hobgoblins (chimerical beings) escape from it. The world does not know them, but changelings do and can interact with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:51:53-07:00","id":289034,"title":"","content":"I think the Chimerical Reality could be easily handled by making it kinda like Twilight - mechanically, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T11:35:31-07:00","id":289785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think a CtL setting with our world, arcadia,the hedge .. but, the Hedge is the dreaming and Hobgoblins (chimerical beings) escape from it. The world does not know them, but changelings do and can interact with them. </div> </div> </div>Some type of hobgoblins learned how to possess human bodies and it stuck, them incarnating to new bodies after death. However, with time the 'soul' of hobgoblin runs risk of diluting and effectively becoming more and more human like until the hobgoblin is convinced he is normal human who recovered from delusion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T20:49:24-07:00","id":297752,"title":"","content":"Changeling: The Lost Dream <br /> Seeming: The Kiths from CtD<br /> Kiths: The Kiths from CtL<br /> Example: Seeming: Sidhe Kith: Shadowsoul <br /> Being creatures of dreams, they are not as stuck in concepts. <br /> Court: Seelie and Unseelie<br /> A human is born with a fae soul. During the crystasis, the human's true fae nature emerges. There is no Chimerical self. changelings are living dream, but the mask hides them from mortal eyes. <br /> The Hedge is the boundary between earth and the Dreaming. Chimerical reality is in, but is separate from mundane reality. The troll is really as big as he is, and cannot fit in the Volkswagen. <br /> use the wyrd system and Contracts <br /> Glamour is as in CtL","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T14:19:09-07:00","id":299267,"title":"","content":"At this point in the development of the White Wolf properties, I\u2019d like to see the developers hold off on a Changeling Translation Guide until after the latest editions of Dreaming and Lost are both published. I <i>absolutely</i> think that such a guide is doable, if you focus primarily on things like \u201chow to run <b>Dreaming</b>, but with Contracts instead of Cantrips\u201d or \u201chow to run Lost, but with the Mists instead of the Mask\u201d; but especially with some of the changes that are occurring between Lost 1e and Lost 2e, a Translation Guide is going to be very different depending on which edition of Lost it\u2019s translating for: compare 1e\u2019s Seemings-and-Kiths hierarchal model with 2e\u2019s Seemings-and-Kiths dual-axis model. Likewise with Dreaming 2e vs. C20: though it\u2019s a 20th Anniversary Edition and thus is less likely to make the sorts of drastic changes we\u2019re going to be seeing in Lost 2e, I fully expect that C20 will be the most radically changed of the 20th Anniversary games. And until we know how both games are going to turn out, it\u2019s going to be hard to decide how aanslation guide will turn out. <br /> <br /> All that said, I did a proof-of-concept Changeling Translation Guide a while back, which unfortunately was lost with the old wikis; so I\u2019ve got some practical experience on how a Translation Guide could work. Break each game down into its component pas, and do a compare-and-contrast of each component one by one; then provide suggestions for how each component might be incorporated into the other game, assuming everything else remains the same. <br /> <br /> For instance, what might CtL look like if it had Childlings, Wilders, and Grumps instead of Beasts, Darklings, Elementals, Fairest, Ogres, and Wizened? What might C20 look like if it had Beasts, Darklings, Elementals, Fairest, Ogres, and Wizened instead of Childlings, Wilders, and Grumps? How do CtL2e\u2019s Kiths compare to C20\u2019s Kiths? <br /> <br /> Another example: how does C20\u2019s concept of Banality compare to CtL2e\u2019s concept of Clarity? How might you hack C20 so that it uses Clarity instead of Banality? How might you hack CtL2e so that it uses Banality instead of Clarity? How does C20\u2019s take on Glamour compare to CtL2e\u2019s Wyrd-and-Glamour? <br /> <br /> Another example: C20\u2019s Dreaming vs. CtL2e\u2019s Hedge and Skein. Again, compare and contrast, and picture what each game might look like if it used the other game\u2019s cosmology, but was otherwise unchanged. <br /> <br /> Seelie/Unseelie Courts vs. Seasonal Courts. Houses vs. Entitlements. Cantrips vs. Contracts, pledges, oneiromancy, and talecrafting (assuming those are all still things in CtL2e). There are lots of parallels to work with. <br /> <br /> I also noted that, settingwise, each game already has in it a <i>very rough</i> analog of the other game\u2019s protagonists: in Lost, we\u2019ve got Charlatans; in Dreaming, we\u2019ve got that bit of backstory where the Resurgence resulted in mortals being taken to Arcadia as their lives were co-opted by the returning Sidhe. If you wanted to port either game\u2019s protagonists whole cloth (more or less) into the other game in a manner where they coexist with the existing protagonists instead of supplanting them, you could do so \u2014 though the relations between the two games\u2019 protagonists would tend to be contentious in both cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T14:21:25-07:00","id":299268,"title":"","content":"If it were me, I would seperate the concepts of Seemings between the games more thoroughly. Seemings and Kiths in Lost seem to combine to make Kiths in Dreaming...Seemings in Dreaming seems it's own concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /